1. Upstream Raw Material Logistics & Throughput
1.1 Feedstock Sourcing & Mass Balance
Primary Resource: Coal Combustion Residuals (CCR) from active utility dry-storage landfills and legacy wet impoundments (e.g., Little Broad Run Landfill, Ohio River Corridor).
Daily Design Throughput: 600 tons per day (TPD) nominal raw dry ash equivalent.
Logistics Routing (The Downhill Production Loop):
Haul trucks load raw CCR at the ridge landfill face.
Payloads move downhill via existing private access roads to the valley-floor processing circuit, using gravity to reduce diesel consumption and transmission wear.
Empty haulers return uphill with zero payload, preserving fast cycle times and eliminating surface-liner puncture risks on the active landfill cap.
